THIRD PARTY DATA SOURCES AND LICENSING

This tool retrieves from external databases. The licence of the OUTPUT depends on
which columns you keep.

KEGG (https://www.kegg.jp)
  Academic use is free. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A LICENCE from Pathway Solutions.
  Any output carrying KO identifiers, KEGG pathway or module IDs, or KEGG gene IDs
  is KEGG-derived. This includes gene_ko_map.csv, kegg_anchor_table.tsv, and the KO
  columns of proteins_anchored.tsv.

UniProt (https://www.uniprot.org)
  CC BY 4.0. Sequences, taxonomy and annotation are freely usable with attribution.
  proteins.fasta and taxonomy_mapping.tsv carry no commercial restriction.

Europe PMC / NCBI E-utilities
  Metadata is freely usable. Full text licensing varies per article. This tool
  retrieves titles and abstracts only.

Pfam / InterPro
  CC0. No restriction.

PRACTICAL CONSEQUENCE
  Dropping the KO and KEGG columns leaves a freely usable commercial asset built on
  UniProt and Pfam. If you need KO annotation commercially, licence KEGG, or
  substitute InterPro and TIGRFAM for the enzyme families and antiSMASH for
  biosynthetic gene clusters.
